In article <1993May7.191216.1374@ugle.unit.no> hafting@Lise.Unit.NO (Helge Hafting) writes:

   Don't worry, the luck/loadstones are so easy to tell apart:
   spoiler follows:
















































   When you find a gray stone, kick it.  A luckstone will move like other rocks/gems,
   a loadstone is too heavy and you'll get "thump" or perhaps "ouch!" and the stone
   won't move.
   You may have to dig around the stone if it is located in the end of a corridor.
   Once you find a luckstone, identify or #name it.  After that, all gray stones
   are loadstones.


I once had this strange problem, that I have been wondering about ever
since. I was playing 3.0 (but I figure it still applies in 3.1), made
it to the castle, and in the corner of the gem room was this gray
stone. I hadn't found either luck or load earlier, so I didn't know
what this one was. As it lay in the corner, kicking didn't work.
Neither did I have a wand of teleport. And digging isn't possible on
the castle level. So what was I to do? (Assuming I didn't dare pick it
up on chance)
